    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d111">

                <pb facs="0180" n="1014" xml:id="pg1014"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/6676</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Consular Officers in Latin American
                            Countries
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Circular telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-18T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 18, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Decline to certify invoices for persons or firms whose names are on enemy trading
                    list and for persons known to be acting as cloaks for said listed firms except
                    where it is alleged that shipment is covered by license of War Trade Board.
                    Sales of local branches of firms in United States to firms on enemy trading list
                    are not to be objected to when alleged to have been duly licensed. All firms
                    suspected of misrepresentation should be promptly reported. Like treatment
                    should be accorded to firms alleging possession British or French [or
                        Italian<anchor n="1" xml:id="d111-f1"/>] license.</p>
                <p>Notify all consular officials.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d111-f1" n="1" xml:id="d111-f1-content">
                <p>Added in accordance with circular telegram of March 9, 1918 (File No.
                    763.72112/6676 Suppl.).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
